1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:04,100
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,221
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,740
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,917
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,420
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,697
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,737
We came to this new world believing That

11
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,817
surely someday we just might find the way.

12
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,297
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,997
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,820
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,617
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,157
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,877
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up, way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,982
A brat who turned into a dragon?

54
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:36,460
I mean, the boy

55
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:38,977
How did you know about that, young lady?

56
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:41,377
Well, to tell the truth,
I saw it all happen.

57
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,837
But I decided not to
tell anybody about it,

58
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,449
because we weren't
supposed to be in there.

59
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,077
We came here on the same boat.

60
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,877
When I saw him change, it scared me.

61
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,254
I'm worried about him.

62
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,280
Oh, I see.

63
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,977
There's no need for you to worry.

64
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:55,890
He's fine.

65
00:02:55,973 --> 00:02:57,313
This laboratory is big,

66
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:59,537
and it's got lots of treatment
rooms scattered throughout it.

67
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:02,597
He's just being kept in a different
part of the lab, that's all.

68
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,510
Oh, really?

69
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,112
Do you know if he's had something to eat?

70
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:08,997
I don't know why but he
wouldn't even touch his food,

71
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,077
yeah, we got him to start eating again.

72
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:14,417
Don't you worry about him;
he's doing just fine now.

73
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,037
Listen, whatever you do,

74
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,537
don't tell anyone about the
boy of the secret room—not

75
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:20,457
even the other kids—it'll
be our little secret,

76
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,370
okay.

77
00:03:21,453 --> 00:03:22,283
Hey, what's

78
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:25,697
the big idea, bird lady?

79
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:28,377
How do you like my 10 layer igloo?

80
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:32,117
Quite a bit thicker than the
last one, isn't it? You see,

81
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,417
it's much harder to break through the snow

82
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:36,337
walls when they're layered
on top of one another.

83
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:39,477
You're just trying to
buy time, aren't you?

84
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,377
This thing can't hold me—you're right.

85
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:45,717
In fact, you could probably break through
all the snow walls in a matter of seconds.

86
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:48,077
If you agree, then why even father?

87
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:52,577
There's no way that I'm losing to you.

88
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,497
That's a good point.

89
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:59,297
Struggle as I may; I have no chance
of ever beating you. However,

90
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:06,297
sometimes it's the smartest,

91
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,617
not the strongest, who wins the fight.

92
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,530
You can't push

93
00:04:09,613 --> 00:04:16,420
me

94
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:22,170
away now

95
00:04:22,253 --> 00:04:24,257
that I've got you in my embrace.

96
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:27,157
You no longer have the
strength to break free.

97
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:33,237
Slowly but surely, my icy body will drain
your power until there's nothing left.

98
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:36,797
Eventually, your heart will freeze.

99
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,337
Would you look at that?

100
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:41,557
It's snowing heavily all around you.

101
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,597
It feels good, doesn't it?

102
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,537
Now slowly

103
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:51,137
close your eyes.

104
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:52,600
close your eyes

105
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,820
There you go.

106
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:57,280
Just relax.

107
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,160
Shut up!

108
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,980
Through the floor?

109
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,860
What tremendous power he has.

110
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:19,137
But that tumble is going to land
him in the trash chute which

111
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:22,677
leads straight to the garbage
dump that's deep underground.

112
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:26,317
He won't be able to make it up
here again unless he could fly.

113
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,720
He dug his own grave so to speak.

114
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:30,640
So long?

115
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,620
You've got to listen to me.

116
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,034
You can't eat anymore.

117
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:51,680
It's bad for you I know it's
hard, but resist the temptation

118
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,960
I need you to believe me.

119
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,652
You've got to be strong.

120
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,281
You're not getting past me, kids.

121
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,497
I'm not going to let you go
back inside the distant room.

122
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,237
You're just eating a little bit.

123
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:04,217
No, you can't.

124
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,000
Let go, you're hurting me.

125
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:07,300
Are you okay?

126
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:09,717
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to hurt you.

127
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,682
Get out of our way, you monster.

128
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:13,480
We want our candy.

129
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,220
This won't work.

130
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,457
I can't stop them without hurting them.

131
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,680
Here's our jam!

132
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,312
Get to the biscuit room!

133
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,490
No, stop!

134
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,312
Stay out of there, kids!

135
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:30,370
Uh-oh.

136
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,877
The effects of the rumble
ball are wearing off!

137
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,120
Now we can eat all the candy!

138
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:44,690
Hurry!

139
00:06:44,773 --> 00:06:45,997
Let's go back to the biscuit room!

140
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,860
I can't wait to have some!

141
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,230
No!

142
00:06:49,313 --> 00:06:50,740
That stuff's bad for you!

143
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,880
What'll I do?

144
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,689
I'm so weak, I can't move.

145
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,880
Whoa. You okay?

146
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:03,570
Bobanosuke!

147
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,640
Where are you?

148
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,980
I'm glad you're here.

149
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:09,020
I can't handle them alone.

150
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,017
You want to tell us
what's going on, buddy?

151
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:13,257
Caesar Cloud's trying to
turn the four children into

152
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:16,517
giants because he wants them
all to become vicious soldiers.

153
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:19,365
And he's doing it by
giving them drugged candy.

154
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:23,457
You've got to stop the kids before
they can consume any more of it!

155
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:26,077
The biscuit room's down
the hall to the left.

156
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,042
That's where they get the candy.

157
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:31,257
There's a girl named Mocha
who's been helping me.

158
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:34,077
She's the only child
who's in their right mind.

159
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:37,677
We've been working together to keep the
others from getting back in the room,

160
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,240
but now she's in danger.

161
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,992
She's been protecting the
candy, and she's all by herself!

162
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:45,780
We made it!

163
00:07:47,420 --> 00:07:48,250
Candy!

164
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,375
We gotta help, Mocha!

165
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:53,400
Mil-flu, gigantesco model!

166
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,860
Get out of the way!

167
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:03,417
I'm afraid I can't hold
them off much longer.

168
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:06,912
They sure are determined to
get their hands on that stuff!

169
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:08,970
Mocha!

170
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,740
Give us candy!

171
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:18,160
You can't have any, can't you
see it's bad for you? Candy! Yay!

172
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,997
I'm telling you guys this
is what's making us sick!

173
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:21,910
Yeah, Dad!

174
00:08:21,993 --> 00:08:23,274
Look what did they do!

175
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:27,097
We asked Chopper and his friends to
help us get out of this place, remember?

176
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,400
It's mine! Give it!

177
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:31,817
No, you gotta listen to them
or we'll never get back home!

178
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:33,717
It's no use, they're too strong!

179
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,800
Let go and run!

180
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:36,620
No, no, I can't!

181
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:41,450
Chase her!

182
00:08:41,533 --> 00:08:45,417
Hey, I'll tell you pretty things
we've got to be in the mouth, Dad!

183
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,330
What?

184
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,939
Yes, it's blocked.

185
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:52,080
You don't have to worry
about a thing, Mocha, dear.

186
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:58,960
It's Monet!

187
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:02,680
Wait, who the hell is she? Ah! It's her!

188
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,982
She's the crazy bird woman
I told you guys about!

189
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:09,300
Mocha, you shouldn't hog all of the candy.

190
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:12,821
Be a nice girl and share
it with the others, okay?

191
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,180
Dammit, Vroom!

192
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,900
Now my heart, come back to me!

193
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:54,080
Here's the counter-shock!

194
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,860
I have a message from Joker.

195
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:05,940
He said that it's a shame.

196
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:07,954
My attack didn't work.

197
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,237
I knew exactly how to get
my heart back from Caesar.

198
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,097
I didn't expect to see you here.

199
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:15,217
I should have guessed you were his lackey.

200
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,359
Don't you have better things to do?

201
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:19,960
Well, Fargo? Mr. Fargo!

202
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,216
I'm kinda in the middle of something.

203
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,100
Does it have to be now?

204
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,900
Vice Admiral Smoker.

205
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,590
Whatever.

206
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,037
Been mean to kill you.

207
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:38,944
Might as well get it over with.

208
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,860
Go ahead and try.

209
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,633
The sooner, the better.

210
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,977
I can only look at trash for so long.

211
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:47,420
before I have to take it out.

212
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:52,080
Especially filthy pirates like you.

213
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,620
What are those?

214
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:01,720
They look mighty ominous.

215
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:06,080
They are, but that's not your business.

216
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:08,820
There you go.

217
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:14,320
I don't want the rank and file to
know the truth about you. Got it?

218
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:18,400
These men, they look up
to you like a father.

219
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:23,900
If they find out that you're
a traitor, they'll be crushed.

220
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,900
Well, too late now.

221
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:27,260
They know it all.

222
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,580
I saw them moments ago.

223
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:32,580
What did you do to them? You'll see.

224
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,230
Vergo!

225
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,700
It looks like I hit a nerve.

226
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,772
Why are you getting so worked up, Smoker?

227
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:45,646
Don't tell me you're actually concerned
about the welfare of those Navy misfits.

228
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,360
I am a base commander.

229
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:52,153
I can do what I want to my
good-for-nothing subordinates.

230
00:11:54,820 --> 00:11:58,879
It's a shame it had to end this way,
but now that you know my secret,

231
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,021
I must kill you.

232
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:27,741
I don't even care if you
are their base commander.

233
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:31,797
Cause once a unit leaves the base.

234
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:35,527
It's their commander who's
responsible for keeping them alive.

235
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:37,257
I'm warning you.

236
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:39,960
Don't ever lay a hand on my men.

237
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,400
No way! What happened?

238
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,991
There's no place to step!

239
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:53,860
The whole place is burning
up! What now? Let's hurry!

240
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,511
Grab the injured and run!

241
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,297
Okay, come on, men!

242
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:58,937
We've got to protect Toshiki!

243
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:00,737
What do you think you're doing?

244
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:01,817
Don't agree with it!

245
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:03,840
He's our foe! What?

246
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:05,540
That's total crap!

247
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,817
Pirates are free to love who they want!

248
00:13:07,900 --> 00:13:11,597
I gotta admit, Blackleg, You look so
cool fighting fake Vergo back there.

249
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:14,437
Then watching you blast him like
that made my heart skip a beat.

250
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,817
Yeah, that was pretty sexy if you ask me.

251
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,220
Hey, shut your traps.

252
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,257
You're not really helping
me out here, you know.

253
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:22,037
Stop acting like he's your friend.

254
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,708
Don't forget he's a pirate.

255
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,560
Whoa, the tank just exploded.

256
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:29,020
And it smoked fire.

257
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:31,440
Crap, not good.

258
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,600
It busted a hole in the wall.

259
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,257
Damn, another explosion.

260
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:41,700
What the hell is going on? Come on! Hurry!

261
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:43,539
What's the matter?

262
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,094
See that purple stuff?

263
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,398
It's the poisonous gas from outside!

264
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:49,880
Start running if you want to live!

265
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,520
The gas is traveling fast!

266
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:59,337
It won't be long before the
whole building is filled!

267
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,250
Get off!

268
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:01,470
Dumbass!

269
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:03,170
Go!

270
00:14:03,253 --> 00:14:04,397
Keep running, Tashigi!

271
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,297
You can't stop to think or you'll die!

272
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,417
Get out of here as fast as possible!

273
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,940
Move! Blackleg! Let's go, men!

274
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:13,727
Pick up the pace or
you're not gonna make it!

275
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:19,200
I didn't have to lift a finger.

276
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:23,048
And look, those fools brought
land of the dead inside for me.

277
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:26,360
But it's too soon.

278
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,340
My life demonstration is not done yet.

279
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,460
You, listen up!

280
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:35,397
Close the gates to C and
D! Yes, sir. What about R?

281
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,660
Keep that one open.

282
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:41,947
Can't have them getting lost, so we'll
lure them to the building's first floor.

283
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:47,100
They're looking for gate R-66, and
the layout of this lab is confusing.

284
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,917
We wouldn't want them going the wrong way.

285
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,294
So we'll just have to guide them there.

286
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:58,910
Curses.

287
00:14:58,993 --> 00:15:00,820
I loathe this stupid secret room.

288
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,900
Too bad, right?

289
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:08,380
But once we're done, I'll be free and
I'll never have to come here again

290
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:11,877
The Straw Hats have
overstayed their welcome.

291
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:15,140
I'd say it's time for them
to be properly punished

292
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,180
I've got Joker on my side,

293
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:21,077
and now I have the opportunity
to kill all of them

294
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:24,940
in the ideal manner Master
we're awaiting orders.

295
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,180
We're ready for combat Yes,

296
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:30,777
but may I ask why you've summoned
us here to Vega punks former

297
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:34,757
command room Wasn't he responsible
for the accident four years ago?

298
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:37,257
We've got a score to settle with him, too.

299
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:38,170
Let's get him.

300
00:15:38,340 --> 00:15:41,417
Why are we wasting time standing
around here staring at each other?

301
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,300
I mean, should we be fighting?

302
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,440
No, not yet.

303
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,800
You gentlemen are my backup plan.

304
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:53,500
You're the best soldiers I have,
so I cannot risk losing you.

305
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,460
Oh, Master.

306
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:59,740
Now, allow me to explain
the plan to all of you.

307
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:04,880
As I said before, once the gates
to C and D have been closed,

308
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,337
the only open routes
through the laboratory

309
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:10,060
will lead to the first
floor of building R,

310
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:12,420
which is directly beneath us.

311
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:16,280
The Straw Hats, G5, the children,

312
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,237
it doesn't matter whether
they're friend or foe,

313
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:22,657
all of the survivors in the lab
will be forced into that room.

314
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:26,622
The first floor has external vents
which can bring in outside air.

315
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:30,137
In other words, we'll be able to
fill the room with land of the dead.

316
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:32,455
There'll be no way for them to escape!

317
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:35,660
They'll be stuck breathing that air!

318
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,080
It'll be like a giant gas chamber!

319
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,800
And soon, they will all die!

320
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:44,337
The best part is we'll be
broadcasting it so my shadow

321
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:47,420
brokers in the new world
can witness the slaughter.

322
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,180
Then they'll respect me!

323
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:51,140
They'll know my greatness!

324
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:59,400
I hate to ask this, but Master Caesar,

325
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:03,420
I don't mean to doubt you or anything,

326
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:06,540
sir, but did you create
the deadly poison gas?

327
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,998
Forgive me, Master.

328
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,400
It seems a lot like Vegapunk's gas,

329
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:14,380
the one from the accident four
years ago, and thing is, Master,

330
00:17:14,660 --> 00:17:15,700
it freaks us out.

331
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,280
Just allow me to explain everything!

332
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:23,290
Please, men!

333
00:17:23,373 --> 00:17:24,203
That day!

334
00:17:24,286 --> 00:17:25,600
It still haunts me!

335
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:29,400
Oh, how I tried to stop the mad scientist!

336
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,290
No!

337
00:17:31,373 --> 00:17:33,977
What if this dangerous
weapon exploded, I cried!

338
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:37,472
Just think of all the innocent
people who would be killed!

339
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:40,040
Please, Vegapunk, don't do this!

340
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,660
But there was no stopping him.

341
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:52,637
and now he's the head of the
navy science division and

342
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,937
he's widely considered the
world's greatest scientist.

343
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:57,217
It's not fair.

344
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:59,057
It should have been me.

345
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:01,797
I cannot accept it.

346
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:06,397
How could someone so heartless come
to be praised as the best of all?

347
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,877
Tell me after what he's
done—does he still?

348
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:11,607
still I'll deserve to
be called the greatest!

349
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:20,480
That's why I must prove him wrong!

350
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:23,477
I don't want to create
a weapon of mass murder,

351
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:26,537
but I'm afraid it must be
done in order to prove I am.

352
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,540
the greatest scientist in the world!

353
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,240
Please, trust me!

354
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:39,877
Once the navy realizes that I
deserve to be their lead scientist.

355
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:46,280
Then I'll be fulfilled and I shall use
my knowledge to bring peace and unity.

356
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:54,997
Master, forgive me, master you're
right; how could I doubt you?

357
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,897
I'm sorry, me too.

358
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:59,257
You are the god of salvation.

359
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:01,937
Don't do it, Caesar.

360
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:03,437
Stop it!

361
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,417
I'm warning you.

362
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,357
Shut it down!

363
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,937
You're putting everyone
on the island in danger.

364
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:11,077
You realize if that weapon explodes,
innocent life will be lost.

365
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:11,990
Shut up!

366
00:19:12,073 --> 00:19:14,417
Ignorant fool—this is a
military testing site.

367
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:15,917
This is my job.

368
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:16,837
Back off!

369
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:21,317
As you may know, the navy wants to kill
as many pirates as they possibly can.

370
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:24,837
I'm simply creating a new weapon
for them, designed to do just that.

371
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:25,750
It's dangerous.

372
00:19:25,833 --> 00:19:27,537
I'm sure your weapon will kill pirates,

373
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:30,357
but you know what else it'll
do—kill a bunch of civilians, idiot!

374
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:35,017
See that's something
called collateral damage.

375
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:38,417
If they don't evacuate,
they deserve what's coming.

376
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,697
Wipe them all out, and we'll
finally have world peace.

377
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:42,620
How could

378
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:44,237
you say that, Caesar?

379
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,357
You're so what you think?

380
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:49,517
I'm cruel perhaps, but so are you?

381
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:51,380
are you Think about it.

382
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,677
You're using the prisoners
as your guinea pigs.

383
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:54,701
Let's be honest.

384
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:57,391
Is there really a difference between them?

385
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:58,390
I think not.

386
00:19:58,473 --> 00:20:03,240
Fleet Admiral Sengoku may be soft, but
Admiral Aka-Inu, on the other hand,

387
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:05,920
I bet he would love one of my weapons.

388
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,240
Now, scram!

389
00:20:07,420 --> 00:20:09,655
I don't need you interrupting my work.

390
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:14,217
Vegapunk's just jealous,
and I can't blame him.

391
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,240
I am a genius.

392
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:20,074
Besides, his silly human enlargement
experiment is nothing but a failure.

393
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,557
You need to be a real magician to make the

394
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:25,237
human body grow that much
in such a short time.

395
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:27,160
I tried to tell him what to do.

396
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:29,380
What he needs is children.

397
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:30,837
Those who are growing.

398
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,117
And fill them with drugs.

399
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:33,965
I believe that's the only way.

400
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,337
What do you think you're doing?

401
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:41,714
Don't try to fight us.

402
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:46,173
I'm almost finished making a weapon
so powerful it's beyond comprehension.

403
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:49,957
Vegapunk, I demand to
know the meaning of this.

404
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:52,557
You've been terminated from
the science division, Caesar.

405
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:54,577
You've gone too far this time.

406
00:20:54,660 --> 00:20:56,417
I can't cover for you anymore.

407
00:20:56,500 --> 00:21:00,457
You gotta be killing me.

408
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:02,200
No, don't do it, Caesar.

409
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,037
Closing the gate between C and B.

410
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:15,820
The gate between D and B is now closed.

411
00:21:17,220 --> 00:21:18,050
That's it.

412
00:21:18,133 --> 00:21:22,335
The passageways between buildings B,
C, and D have been secured, Master.

413
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:25,180
Come on, run like hell, you guys!

414
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:37,080
Hold on, you can talk!

415
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,600
Who the hell are you?

416
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:43,740
I, uh...

417
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:49,860
Who am I?

418
00:21:50,260 --> 00:21:52,966
I am the one who should
be asking that of you!
